  <p>
    The worktree appears under the repo in the sidebar. You can click on it to view its
    details, including the worktree path, branch name, and any running tasks.
  </p>

  <h2>Create a worktree via the CLI</h2>

  <p>
    Use the <code>band worktrees create</code> command to create a worktree from your terminal:
  </p>

  <pre><code>band worktrees create my-app feat/login</code></pre>

  <p>
    This creates a new branch called <code>feat/login</code> in the <code>my-app</code> repo
    and sets up a worktree directory for it. The command returns the path to the new worktree.
  </p>

  <p>
    To branch from a specific base branch instead of the default:
  </p>

  <pre><code>band worktrees create my-app feat/login --base develop</code></pre>

  <p>
    You can also create a worktree and immediately submit a task to start the agent working:
  </p>

  <pre><code>band worktrees create my-app feat/auth --prompt "Implement JWT authentication for the API"</code></pre>

  <p>
    This is the recommended workflow for most cases &mdash; it creates the worktree and
    dispatches a task in a single step.
  </p>

  <h2>Setup scripts</h2>

  <p>
    If your repo contains a <code>.band/config.json</code> file with a <code>setup</code>
    script, Band runs it automatically after creating the worktree. This is useful for
    installing dependencies or performing other initialization:
  </p>

  <pre><code set:html={`{
  "setup": "npm install",
  "teardown": "rm -rf node_modules"
}`}></code></pre>

  <p>
    Setup scripts run inside the worktree directory. If a setup script fails, the worktree is
    still created &mdash; the failure is non-fatal and reported in the dashboard.
  </p>

  <h2>Worktree isolation</h2>

  <p>
    Each worktree is fully isolated. An agent working in one worktree cannot affect files in
    another worktree or on your main branch, so you can safely run multiple agents in parallel:
  </p>

  <pre><code>band worktrees create my-app feat/auth --prompt "Add authentication"
band worktrees create my-app feat/search --prompt "Add full-text search"
band worktrees create my-app fix/perf --prompt "Optimize database queries"</code></pre>

  <h2>Listing and removing worktrees</h2>

  <p>To see all worktrees, or filter by repo:</p>

  <pre><code>band worktrees list
band worktrees list my-app</code></pre>

  <p>
    When you are done with a worktree, remove it to clean up the worktree directory and branch:
  </p>

  <pre><code>band worktrees remove my-app feat/login</code></pre>

  <h2>Next step</h2>

  <p>
